# autotune-lsb: Auto Tune multimode (issue #205) in LSB - the mirrored sideband.
#
# Same rule as `autotune-usb` (suggest, never move before the second press), on
# the other sideband: the fixture is in LSB with the mirrored real filter
# (-3000..0 Hz, the mapping of src/cfg/mode.c::update_real_filters() that
# mocks/mock_radio.c publishes) and the TEST-ONLY voice mass sits 2850 Hz BELOW
# the dial, so the estimated shift is -752 Hz. The sign of the suggestion follows
# the dial: a negative shift lowers the VFO.
#
# scenario_settle codifies the mirror: the dial must not have moved after the
# COLLECT window (the session stays in PREVIEW; a suggestion that retuned the
# voice would show the dial on start - 752). The mirrored sign is checked on the
# source by the native test with synthetic spectra (where the exact value is
# observable); the bank pins the fact that no write happens.

name autotune-lsb
screen autotune-lsb

seed 20

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 96000

mode lsb
filter_low 0
filter_high 3000
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
